<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Moorcroft</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1767">1767</a>–<a href="/years/1825">1825</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Moorcroft was an English veterinary surgeon and explorer who managed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>'s horse stud in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>. In search of horses he travelled through the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalaya</a>, Ladakh and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>, and from 1819 led a long expedition through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a>. He died on the return journey in northern Afghanistan in 1825; his travels were published in 1841.</p></div>
